hot-1 — Profile & attribute the ASDF load/compile (plan-3; DO FIRST, gates all 3 plans).

Measure before optimizing.  Establishes the baseline every other issue reports against.

WHAT
- Instrument the load path with cheap phase timers (a small ring of named counters,
  printed on demand): time spent in READ (the reader), MACROEXPAND-ALL, EVAL of
  top-level forms, and CLOS setup (defclass/defmethod/make-instance/dispatch).  Also
  count: forms read, symbols interned, conses allocated, funcalls, GC time.
- Drive (require :asdf) (or the closest reproducible load) three ways where possible
  — source, text fasl, and later binary fasl — and dump the attribution.
- Add an eval-hot-path micro-profiler: sample or count time in variable lookup
  (environment_find_variable), argument-list construction, funcall dispatch, and the
  DIVOP/arith fast paths — to confirm the ~150us/funcall breakdown on THIS workload.
- Optionally a build flag BOCL_PROFILE that compiles in the counters (off by default,
  zero cost when off).

DELIVERABLE: a written baseline table (phase -> seconds/%, on a named machine) in the
issue, so plan-1/2/3 each cite "before/after" against it.  This tells us whether the
lever is the reader, the macroexpander, the evaluator, or CLOS — and thus how much of
each plan matters.

ACCEPTANCE: reproducible attribution of the ASDF load and compile times; numbers
recorded; zero overhead when BOCL_PROFILE is off; suite green.

DEPENDS ON: none (first thing to do across the whole performance program).
